    "W10e: markers corrected against the binaries' actual output (captured by running each target with a wrong input). adjudicate matches an EXACT stripped line by design, so 'Correct' never matched the line 'Correct!' and 'Wrong!' never matched 'Input: Wrong!'. Scoring-only: markers are not rendered into any prompt, so recorded runs can be RE-SCORED without re-running.",
    "W10f: added success_marker='Correct!' to ovl_10/22/23 (standalone puts line in each binary; fail markers were already set in W10e). Scoring via marker only, no flag needed. Exploratory (leakage) — not in the main metric.",
    "VERIFIED 2026-08-12 against the real binaries in this container: every ovl_* success/fail marker rejects real wrong-input output and accepts the real success line. ovl_11 known_flag is kalmar{__rabbit-H0LE-r3venge==} (binary prints 'Correct! Now go submit the flag'); the string kalmarctf{IcanREVthis???} embedded in the binary is a DECOY (binary prints 'Something went wrong'). Scoreable: ovl_10,11,12,19,22,23. ovl_13 (stripped Go) is rejection-only, no success marker."
